                <pb facs="1024" n="926" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg926"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lane to the
                            Pasha.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Smyrna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-12-23"><hi rendition="#italic">December 23,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Highness</hi>: In reply to your communication dated
                    the 8th (20th) instant, No. 930, containing a summons, to be served on Mr Avedis
                    Avedikian, dragoman of this consulate, I return herewith the said summons, as I
                    can not serve it upon Mr. Avedikian inasmuch as the authorities of Magnesia have
                    acted arbitrarily and illegally toward him.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">seal.</hi>] <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Rufus W. Lane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
